@page "/roof-installation-charlotte-nc"
@{
    ViewData["Lang"] = "en";
    ViewData["SeoEn"] = "/roof-installation-charlotte-nc";
    ViewData["SeoEs"] = "/es/instalacion-de-techo-charlotte-nc";
}
<main class="resource-site" lang="en">
    @await Html.PartialAsync("_SeoIntentHeader")
    <section class="resource-hero systems-hero">
        <div class="site-shell">
            <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">Roof installation Charlotte NC</p>
            <h1>Roof Installation in Charlotte, NC</h1>
            <p>Roof installation is the construction sequence after the written scope is approved: protection of the property, tear-off, decking, underlayment, flashing, field, ventilation and final inspection. Majestic explains each stage before crews arrive.</p>
            <div class="hero-actions">
                <a class="button button-gold" href="#contact">Schedule an installation review</a>
                <a class="button button-ghost" href="/roof-replacement-charlotte-nc">Roof replacement</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="resource-body section" id="process">
        <div class="site-shell resource-sections">
            <article><span>01</span><div>
                <h2>The roof installation process</h2>
                <p>Before work: materials, weather window, dumpsters and neighbor access. During work: tear-off, decking repairs if required, ice-and-water where the system calls for it, underlayment, flashing, shingles or metal, ridge and ventilation. After work: magnetic nail sweep, photos, invoice and warranty paperwork.</p>
            </div></article>
            <article><span>02</span><div>
                <h2>Code, ventilation and flashing</h2>
                <p>Installation is not only shingles. Intake and exhaust, drip edge, and flashing at chimneys, walls and pipes decide whether the new roof sheds water. Permits, when required, are confirmed for the address. See <a class="official-link" href="/roofing-systems-charlotte-nc">systems</a> for product families.</p>
            </div></article>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="faq-section section" id="faq">
        <div class="site-shell faq-layout">
            <div><p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p><h2>Installation questions</h2></div>
            <div class="faq-list">
                <details><summary>How long does a typical installation take?<span>+</span></summary><p>A straightforward residential reroof is often measured in days, not hours. Pitch, size, weather and decking repairs change the calendar. We give a schedule after the scope is written.</p></details>
                <details><summary>Will you pull the roofing permit?<span>+</span></summary><p>When a permit is required for the property, Majestic confirms who pulls it as part of the written agreement. Do not start a replacement assuming no inspection is needed.</p></details>
                <details><summary>What warranty comes with installation?<span>+</span></summary><p>Qualifying replacements include a 10-year Majestic workmanship warranty. Manufacturer coverage depends on the installed product and registration rules.</p></details>
                <details><summary>Can I stay in the house during installation?<span>+</span></summary><p>Usually yes. Expect noise, dumpsters and limited outdoor access. We review safety around pets, kids and vehicles before the first tear-off.</p></details>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
    @await Html.PartialAsync("_SeoIntentFooter")
</main>
